 "summary": "Measured first on a real stack: an objectstack showcase at 299a2c62 plus a production console build of 5a2a6ab, with Playwright counting requests over 4 full reloads of a showcase_task record page. Base sent GET /data/showcase_task/ID twice concurrently, and explain update and delete twice each concurrently, 43-44 API calls per reload. Instrumented caller stacks found 1 caller for the double GET: record:details' DetailView, whose load effect re-runs while its first read is pending because RecordDetailsRenderer rebuilds sections on every render. They found 2 hosts for each explain question: RecordDetailView, and DetailView asking 20-35 ms later. The fix shares the in-flight request at both sources. ObjectStackAdapter.findOne shares by resource+id+params through one private helper, shareInFlight, that find now uses too, with find's behaviour unchanged; a write through emitMutation drops that resource's pending findOne reads. useRecordEditable keeps a pending map beside verdictCache under the same key; a staled question leaves the map, and retainForPrincipal empties it. After the fix, measured the same way: GET ID once, each explain question once, 40 calls per reload on 4 of 4 runs. Neither host file was edited. One reading to confirm: the card's ruling scopes the ?populate= pair out. It is actually RecordDetailView's own $expand record read, sent again in sequence when objectDef changes identity, so a record open still reads the record 3 times as 2 different requests (see open_questions).",
